      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "Suibne the Madman:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "celt/m-airiuclan#Airiuclan.1",
      "source_sha256": "0fb2df667910796c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-12",
      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "My little oratory in Tuaim Inbir, a top of ivy: a fully built house would not be more [?] — with its stars last night, with its sun, with its moon."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "celt/m-airiuclan#Airiuclan.2",
      "source_sha256": "42581cd37a2e8a4e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-12",
      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "Gobbán made that (so that its story may be told to you); my little heart, God from heaven, he is the thatcher who has thatched it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "celt/m-airiuclan#Airiuclan.3",
      "source_sha256": "868169a0129c98c1",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-12",
      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "A house where wet does not rain in, a place where spear-points are not feared; as bright as though in a garden, and it without a fence around it."
    }
  ]
}
